t=open('template_source.html').read()
M={'PVD':('#16334f','Atoms leave a source and fly in straight lines (line-of-sight) to the substrate. Watch the top grow thick while the trench sidewalls stay thin.','Navy atoms are physically ejected or evaporated from the source; no chemical reaction is needed. Raise the angular spread or pressure to scatter more atoms into the trench; raise surface mobility to let atoms settle into a denser film.','Sources: Mattox (2010); Ohring (2002); Thornton & Hoffman (1989).'),
'CVD':('#b5443b','Precursor molecules diffuse in every direction and react on the heated surface, leaving a solid film and gaseous by-products.','Low reaction probability (cooler substrate) lets molecules reach the trench floor: conformal film. High temperature makes them react at the first surface they touch, so the mouth closes and leaves a void. Illustrative activation values.','Sources: Xu et al. (2025); Khare & Singh (2026); Ohring (2002).'),
'ALD':('#1f7f8a','Pulse A, purge, pulse B, purge: each step saturates the surface and adds one layer. Shorten a pulse and the deep trench is left unsaturated.','Dark cells are the chemisorbed layer after pulse A. Try a short pulse in a deep trench, a short purge, or a temperature outside the window (about 150–350 °C thermal, up to about 250 °C plasma) to see why ALD recipes are tuned. Growth per cycle values are indicative.','Sources: George (2010); Puurunen (2005); Johnson et al. (2014); Profijt et al. (2011).')}
for k,(a,sub,note,src) in M.items():
    o=t.replace('__MODE__',k).replace('__ACC__',a).replace('__SUB__',sub).replace('__NOTE__',note+' '+src).replace('__UNIT__','one atomic layer' if k=='ALD' else '1 nm').replace('__TITLE__',k+' thin-film model')
    open(f'{k}_model.html','w').write(o)
